    {
      "id": "1547844608229249094",
      "type": "Default",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-11T05:41:52.164+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "I think there is some basic infrastructure stuff that's broken at the moment?\n\nI tried, as advised by the docs (https://github.com/CarlFK/pici/wiki/Getting-Started) to pick an FPGA, e.g. this one:\nhttps://welland.fpgas.online/fpgas/pi38.html\n\nI built an Arty A7-35T bitstream locally and tried to upload it with the form in the top right. I get a 413 Request Entity Too Large served by nginx, on a 2.1MB .bit file.\n\nSo then I tried to connect via ssh using the `ssh -p 23822 pi@welland.fpgas.online` instruction. No dice, doesn't look like anything is listening on that port.\n\nThen I tried clicking the \"Reset\" button, which I presume is supposed to power cycle the PoE port. It did update the websocket messages to indicate the control socket was cycled, but it didn't affect the state of the LEDs in the video feed at all, and ssh login isn't any more successful.",
      "author": {
        "id": "422557460092551178",
        "name": "storborg",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "storborg",
        "color": null,
